@startuml tui-ai-task-routing-sequence
title TUI AI Task Routing — optional classify -> role -> route

actor User
participant "AiPanel (frame loop)" as Panel
participant "AiPanel thread\n(owns tokio Runtime)" as Thread
participant Sanitizer as San
participant "classify_task_role()" as Classifier
participant "classifier_provider\n(fast/cheap)" as ClassifierProvider
participant "DefaultRouter::chat" as Router
participant "role's provider chain" as Chain

User -> Panel : Enter (input + selection context)
Panel -> Thread : submit(prompt, ctx) via std::sync::mpsc
activate Thread

alt auto_route == false (default)
  Thread -> Thread : role = TaskRole::General
else auto_route == true
  Thread -> San : mask(latest_user_message) [cloud classifier only]
  San --> Thread : masked text
  Thread -> Classifier : classify_task_role(classifier_provider, masked text)
  activate Classifier
  Classifier -> ClassifierProvider : short single-shot completion\n(bounded 5s timeout)
  ClassifierProvider --> Classifier : label or timeout/error
  Classifier --> Thread : TaskRole (falls back to General\non any timeout/error/unparseable label)
  deactivate Classifier
end

Thread -> Thread : route = role_routes[role]\n(falls back to top-level\nprovider_order/default_model\nwhen role has no entry)
Thread -> San : mask(payload) [main request, unchanged from T49]
San --> Thread : masked + placeholder map
Thread -> Router : chat(messages, route.provider_order,\nroute.model_override, tx)
activate Router
Router -> Chain : try_in_order (unchanged T49/r7 logic)
Chain --> Router : ChatDelta stream / final Ok or Err
deactivate Router
Thread -> San : restore_originals(reply, map)
San --> Thread : restored text
Thread --> Panel : Assistant(restored) / Error
deactivate Thread
Panel --> User : render history + ProviderServing\n+ role (when auto_route) + sanitized
@enduml
